<urn:usf:acceptance:provider-task-qualification> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A qualification is produced only from observations bound to real invocations of the exact provider and model named, and an observation set that is incomplete, mismatched, digest-inconsistent or drawn from another route is refused rather than scored. A suite failure leaves the route unqualified. A qualification for one model grants nothing to any other model or provider. The stored qualification is visible to the shared capability model as a task class for that exact route, and to nothing wider. A route that gains a task class gains no economic authorization, and a route with economic authorization gains no task class. No input to, and no field of, a qualification records account tier, quota, billing or console state." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
