<urn:usf:requirement:answer-evidences-one-case> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "One observed answer evidences exactly the case it was produced for. The same answer offered for a second case evidences nothing there, so one generic answer cannot be multiplied into several pieces of evidence, and several graders reading one artefact do not make several independent observations of it." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
