<urn:usf:requirement:grader-is-comparison-not-proof> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "a grade is a comparison result; it is not an observation, an interpretation or a proof." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:grader-is-comparison-not-proof> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:grader-is-comparison-not-proof> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:grader-is-comparison-not-proof> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A grader compares one observed answer against one declared expectation. It observes nothing about the world, interprets nothing, and proves nothing. A passing grade is evidence that an answer matched an expectation and evidence of exactly that; it is never evidence that the requirement the case was written for is met." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:grader-is-comparison-not-proof> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
