<urn:usf:requirement:grader-states-what-it-judges> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "grader competence is declared per kind; a case outside it is INAPPLICABLE, never a silent zero." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:grader-states-what-it-judges> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:grader-states-what-it-judges> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:grader-states-what-it-judges> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Every grader kind declares what it asserts, the mode of judgement it performs, and the requirement dimensions it is competent to judge. A grader asked to judge a dimension it does not declare returns INAPPLICABLE and never a pass or a fail, because a grader that cannot judge a case has established nothing about the answer." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
