<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-carries-no-commercial-claim> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "qualification-carries-no-commercial-claim" <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-carries-no-commercial-claim> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "qualification refuses on suite performance only; economic authorization refuses on economics only; neither substitutes for the other." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-carries-no-commercial-claim> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "The two were previously entangled by implementation rather than by contract: the qualification requirement never asked for quota or cost, and the evaluator demanded them anyway." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-carries-no-commercial-claim> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-carries-no-commercial-claim> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-carries-no-commercial-claim> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "Qualification neither requires nor produces evidence of account tier, remaining quota, billing status, paid-usage configuration, account ownership or provider-console state. Whether a route may be executed at all remains decided by the operator's explicit economic authorization, evaluated where execution is authorised and nowhere else. Neither concept may be read as the other, and no qualification input may be an observation of a commercial account." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-carries-no-commercial-claim> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
