<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-from-observed-invocation> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "qualification-from-observed-invocation" <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-from-observed-invocation> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "every graded answer traces to one recorded invocation of the exact model being qualified; an unbound answer is inadmissible rather than zero-scored." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-from-observed-invocation> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "Scoring an unbound answer as zero would be the wrong repair. A missing answer is a legitimate zero, but an answer of unknown origin is not evidence at all, and admitting it at any score would let a caller decide the outcome." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-from-observed-invocation> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-from-observed-invocation> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-from-observed-invocation> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A task-class qualification is derived only from a set of observations, one per graded suite case, each recording an invocation that actually occurred: the exact provider, the requested and actual model, the transport, the case it answered, the digest of the prompt sent, the answer returned and its digest, the digest of the execution evidence record it came from, and when it happened. An answer that names no observation is not graded. An observation whose recomputed digest does not match its content is refused." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-from-observed-invocation> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-from-observed-invocation> <urn:usf:predicate:verificationClass> <urn:usf:verification-class:dependency-declaration-integrity> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
