<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-scope-is-exact-route> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "one qualification, one provider and model; a mixed observation set is refused." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-scope-is-exact-route> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-scope-is-exact-route> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-scope-is-exact-route> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A qualification is held by one exact provider and model pair and by nothing else. It does not extend to another model from the same provider, to the same model reached through another provider, or to any family, alias or underlying model they share. Every observation in the set must name that same pair, and an observation naming a different pair makes the set inadmissible rather than merely unscored." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-scope-is-exact-route> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-scope-is-exact-route> <urn:usf:predicate:verificationClass> <urn:usf:verification-class:dependency-declaration-integrity> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
