<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-suite-is-authority> <urn:usf:predicate:invariant> "suite identity, corpus identity and policy identity are bound into the qualification digest." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-suite-is-authority> <urn:usf:predicate:requirementSeverity> <urn:usf:requirement-severity:blocking> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-suite-is-authority> <urn:usf:predicate:semanticStage> <urn:usf:stage:validation> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-suite-is-authority> <urn:usf:predicate:text> "A task class means exactly what its suite cases test. The suite and corpus identity and version, the policy identity and version, and the per-dimension thresholds that decide the verdict are all part of qualification identity, so a qualification earned under one suite version is not a qualification under another. Changing what a task class requires is therefore a change to the suite, made where the suite is declared, and not an adjustment inside the evaluator." <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
<urn:usf:requirement:qualification-suite-is-authority> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:Requirement> <urn:usf:graph:provider-task-qualification> .
